VOID retains the library/CMake subset of the official curl 8.23.0 release.
Upstream copyright and permission notices are in COPYING and the source files.
VOID-PROVENANCE.json records the archive URL, SHA-256, signature identity,
retained upstream file hashes and the four corrected private file hashes.

Local modifications: lib/cookie.c, lib/cookie.h and lib/getinfo.c distinguish
failed cookie enumeration allocations (CURLE_OUT_OF_MEMORY) from successful
empty enumeration. The existing share lock, partial-list cleanup, disabled
cookie/HTTP behavior and public ABI are preserved. The exact review diff is
docs/net/http/evidence/curl-8.23.0-cookie-oom-candidate.patch in the VOID tree.

The additional correction in lib/http2.c removes a duplicated HTTP/2 window
increment after the absolute nghttp2 window setter. Its setter error handling,
public ABI and flow-control pause/resume policy remain intact. The exact diff is
docs/net/http/evidence/curl-8.23.0-http2-window-candidate.patch. Approval and
independent before/after receipts are in docs/net/http/HTTP2_WINDOW_REVIEW.md.

Production CMake builds these files directly. No patch application or source
from .toolchains is part of the curl build. .toolchains is disposable storage
for independently pinned transitive dependencies and build tools.

Retained: release top-level files, CMake/, include/, lib/, docs/, scripts/.
Omitted: command-line tool src/, tests/, projects/, m4/. The retained configure
script is provenance material; this subset is built through CMake only.
See cmake/CurlProvider.cmake for the explicit library feature policy.

Upstream follow-up: prepared locally, not submitted. No upstream acceptance
is claimed. The detailed follow-up record is docs/net/http/PATCH_REVIEW.md.
